# Life Admin — Project Memory / AI Context

## Purpose

This file is the persistent project context for AI coding assistants. Read it before making architectural or implementation decisions.

## Product

Life Admin is a personal document and renewal tracker.

The user should be able to manage important documents and quickly understand what needs attention.

## Assignment Constraints

Mandatory direction:
- Next.js 16.
- React.
- Tailwind CSS.
- PostgreSQL or MongoDB; project uses PostgreSQL.
- Git/GitHub.
- Live deployment.
- Validation/security.
- Testing.
- Performance considerations.
- Meaningful real-world functionality.

AI is optional.

## Core Entities

User:
- id
- name
- email
- passwordHash
- createdAt

Document:
- id
- userId
- title
- category
- documentNumber
- issueDate
- expiryDate
- notes
- createdAt
- updatedAt

## Document Categories

- IDENTITY
- INSURANCE
- VEHICLE
- CERTIFICATION
- WARRANTY
- SUBSCRIPTION
- OTHER

## Document Status

- ACTIVE
- EXPIRING_SOON
- EXPIRED
- NO_EXPIRY

Default threshold:
- Expiring Soon = within 30 days.

## Core APIs

POST `/api/documents`
GET `/api/documents`
GET `/api/documents/[id]`
PATCH `/api/documents/[id]`
DELETE `/api/documents/[id]`

Recommended:
GET `/api/dashboard`

## Core Pages

- `/login`
- `/register`
- `/dashboard`
- `/documents`
- `/documents/new`
- `/documents/[id]`
- `/documents/[id]/edit`

## UI Principles

- Mobile-first.
- Dashboard is the primary overview.
- Documents page is the management workspace.
- Desktop uses tables where useful.
- Mobile uses cards.
- Search and filters are first-class controls.
- Status text is always visible.
- Loading/empty/error states are required.

## Security Principle

The authenticated session determines the current user.

Never trust:
- client-provided userId.
- client-provided ownership.
- unvalidated request bodies.

Every document query must be scoped to the authenticated user.

## Validation Principle

Zod is the server-side boundary validator.

The frontend can validate for UX, but backend validation remains authoritative.

## Architecture Principle

Prefer:
UI -> API/Server -> Service -> Prisma -> PostgreSQL

Avoid putting business logic directly into UI components.

## Optional AI

AI may extract structured document fields from user-provided text.

AI output:
1. Parse.
2. Validate with Zod.
3. Show user for review.
4. Save only after validation/confirmation.

AI must never bypass security or validation.

## Definition of Done

A feature must be functional, responsive, validated, secure, appropriately tested, and consistent with the PRD and rules.
